  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday)\nIssued at 937 PM CDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nThursday the cut off low will finally shift eastward as a trough \naxis moves into the Midwest and skies will become partly cloudy \nacross the TN Valley. Will see a low chance (20-30%) of showers \nand thunderstorms mainly east of I-65 Thursday afternoon. A little\nbit higher rain chances on Friday afternoon as the trough axis \nmakes it into the OH Valley and sends a disturbance into the TN \nValley. The sfc low lifts into the Lower Great Lakes while the \nassociated cold front will not make much southern progress, \nremaining up in the OH Valley. Not much of a pattern change over \nthe weekend as it looks like the front will not make it into the \nregion and we will continue to get diurnally driven showers and \nthunderstorms.\n\nTemps will be in the upper 80s to lower 90s Thursday through \nSunday but the heat index will make it feel more like it is in the\nupper 90s to just above 100 degrees. Not reaching heat advisory \nthresholds, however with most of us returning back to school this \nweek, heat safety needs to remain a priority.",
